    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>This Fief unites two older domains: Ventrue-ruled Aquitaine (centered on Bordeaux) and Toreador Occitania (centered on Toulouse, historic seat of France's oldest Toreador lineage, now nearly extinguished). Ventrue Marquis Edouard de Morsac, the last of the old Anglo-Aquitaine Ventrue lineage and architect of Bordeaux's economic prosperity, rules from Bordeaux behind a courteous, reserved public manner that conceals a proud and merciless political operator; many suspect him of having orchestrated the disappearance of the Occitan Toreador line in 1793.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Courteous, reserved, impeccably mannered &mdash; and utterly without mercy the moment your interests are threatened. You let others underestimate the smiling businessman.</p>",
    "notes": "Widely suspected (never proven) of orchestrating the 1793 disappearance of the Occitan Toreador line. Rival of the Brujah Ferdinand, who is secretly a puppet of the Sabbat agent Nathanael.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
